SpmObservables.hpp:423:
    constexpr std::size_t per_lane = 2 * (static_cast<std::size_t>(NCH) + 2) + 21;

Nothing names or derives that 21. It is the hand-count of the take() calls in view(), SpmObservables.hpp:385-403:
    for (const Domain domain : domains)
      output.concentration[domain_index(domain)] = take(static_cast<std::size_t>(NCH + 2) * L);
    for (auto *field : { &output.effective_diffusivity,
                         &output.molar_flux,
                         &output.surface_stoichiometry,
                         &output.exchange_current_density,
                         &output.overpotential,
                         &output.electrode_ocv })
      for (const Domain domain : domains)
        (*field)[domain_index(domain)] = take(L);
    output.entropic_coefficient = take(L);
    ... (nine single-lane takes) ...
    output.total_heat = take(L);
    assert(cursor <= storage_.size());

6*2 + 9 = 21 today, so the arithmetic is correct. But the guard is `assert(cursor <= storage_.size())` at line 404 -- it runs AFTER every subspan has been taken, and `std::span::subspan(offset, count)` is undefined behaviour when `count > size() - offset`. In Release the assert compiles away entirely. Adding one field to BasicSpmObservables (SpmObservables.hpp:340-359) and to view() without bumping the literal 21 yields silent out-of-bounds spans, not a diagnostic.

proposal:
Name the counts once and derive both sides from them, and make take() self-guarding:

  static constexpr std::size_t per_domain_lane_fields = 6;  // effective_diffusivity .. electrode_ocv
  static constexpr std::size_t shared_lane_fields    = 9;   // entropic_coefficient .. total_heat
  static constexpr std::size_t per_lane =
    2 * (static_cast<std::size_t>(NCH) + 2)
    + 2 * per_domain_lane_fields + shared_lane_fields;

  auto take = [&](std::size_t count) {
    assert(count <= storage_.size() - cursor);
    auto result = std::span<Real>{ storage_ }.subspan(cursor, count);
    cursor += count;
    return result;
  };

and end view() with `assert(cursor == static_cast<std::size_t>(active_lanes) * per_lane);` (equality, not `<=`) so an over-count is caught too. Also drop the duplicated `if (n_lanes <= 0) throw ...` at SpmObservables.hpp:420-421: the constructor already ran checked_lane_count (line 411-416) before required_size, because n_lanes_ is declared before storage_. Same class, same check, two different exception messages. Note SpmObservables.hpp:105-115 (SpmTransportCache::checked_shape) and src/core/AgeingKernel.hpp:67-82 (AgeingScratchStorage) are a third and fourth copy of this checked-lane-count/overflow-guard idiom -- one shared `detail::checked_lane_extent(int lanes, std::size_t per_lane)` returning the element count would serve all four.

