CORE CLAIM CONFIRMED, TWO SUB-CLAIMS REFUTED.

Confirmed verbatim. SpmObservables.hpp:423: `constexpr std::size_t per_lane = 2 * (static_cast<std::size_t>(NCH) + 2) + 21;` — the 21 is a bare literal, nothing derives or names it. The hand-count checks out: BasicSpmObservables (340-359) declares 6 PerDomain lane fields (effective_diffusivity, molar_flux, surface_stoichiometry, exchange_current_density, overpotential, electrode_ocv) taken at 387-394 as 6x2=12 single-lane takes, plus 9 shared spans (entropic_coefficient, negative_entropic_coefficient, open_circuit_voltage, resistance, terminal_voltage, reversible_heat, reaction_heat, ohmic_heat, total_heat) at 395-403. 12+9=21. Confirmed the guard is only `assert(cursor <= storage_.size());` at line 404, after every subspan is formed, stripped under NDEBUG.

NOT A LIVE BUG — latent only. view(active_lanes) is reached from SpmPipeline.hpp:294 and :523 as `observables_.view(period)`; lanePeriod (SpmPipeline.hpp:690-716) returns either a divisor of n_lanes_ or `return n_lanes_`, so period <= n_lanes_ always, and observables_ was built with n_lanes_. cursor = L*per_lane <= storage_.size() holds today. The reviewer framed it as a maintenance hazard ("adding one field ... yields silent out-of-bounds"), which is fair. [clarity] is the right tag.

Dead-check claim CONFIRMED. n_lanes_ is declared at 430, storage_ at 431, so checked_lane_count runs before required_size; grep shows required_size has no caller other than the ctor initialiser at 366. Lines 420-421 are unreachable.

REFUTED SUB-CLAIM 1 — "two different exception messages". False. Line 414 and line 421 are byte-identical: `throw std::invalid_argument{ "SPM observable scratch requires at least one lane" };` Same string both times. (AgeingKernel.hpp:70 and :77 are likewise identical to each other.) Harmless to the fix, but the reviewer misread it.

REFUTED SUB-CLAIM 2 — "one shared detail::checked_lane_extent(int lanes, std::size_t per_lane) would serve all four". False for SpmTransportCache::checked_shape (SpmObservables.hpp:105-115). It is not the same idiom: it carries two checks a per_lane-only helper cannot express and returns a struct, not a count:
    if (lanes > std::numeric_limits<int>::max() / 2)
      throw std::length_error{ "SPM transport cache extent is not representable" };
    const auto values = static_cast<std::size_t>(lanes) * 2;
    if (values > std::numeric_limits<std::size_t>::max() / sizeof(real_t))
      throw std::length_error{ "SPM transport cache byte count is not representable" };
