  REQUIRE(core::computeSpmStress(explosive, observables, 1, output) == Status::Numerical_failure);
Case 2 (line 112) tests validateSpmStressParams; case 3 (line 128) tests arena checkpointing. Nothing tests the physics against a value derivable without Cell_SPM, so a shared error in both implementations is invisible, and the quadrature matrix p.integration is only ever exercised at one operating point.

The kernel has a strong analytic invariant. Diffusion-induced stress is driven by the concentration GRADIENT, so a uniform profile must give identically zero hydrostatic stress. Reading SpmStress.hpp:137-158 with c(x) = c0 constant: integral[row] = c0 * Q_row . x^2, so `total` = c0*(I[2N+2] - I[centre]) ~ c0/3 and `partial` = c0*(I[centre+i]-I[centre])/x^3 ~ c0/3 for every i, whence
  radial     = 2*factor/3 * (total - partial)          -> 0
  tangential = factor/3   * (2*total + partial - local) = factor/3 * (2c0/3 + c0/3 - c0) -> 0
and at i == 0, radial = 2*factor/9 * (3*total - c_centre) = 2*factor/9 * (c0 - c0) -> 0. The residual is pure Chebyshev quadrature error in Q, not model error.

proposal:
Add to tests/unit/core_SpmStress_test.cpp, with the band written into the file BEFORE the first run (CLAUDE.md section 3):

TEST_CASE("Dai hydrostatic stress vanishes for a uniform concentration profile",
          "[core][ageing][stress][oracle]")

Build SpmStressParams from Model_SPM as the existing StressReferenceCell::params does, allocate SpmObservableScratch<NCH>{4}, and fill EVERY node of both electrodes in all four lanes with one constant c0 per lane (use four distinct c0, e.g. 5e3, 1.5e4, 2.5e4, 3.0e4, so the case is non-degenerate across lanes -- CLAUDE.md section 4 forbids validating an oracle only on the symmetric case). Then:

  REQUIRE(core::computeSpmStress(params, observables, 4, output) == Status::Success);
  for each domain d, each lane:
    const double scale = params.partial_molar_volume[d] * params.youngs_modulus[d]
                         / (1.0 - params.poisson_ratio[d]) * c0[lane];
    REQUIRE(std::abs(output.dai_maximum_hydrostatic[d][lane]) <= 1e-10 * scale);

REGISTERED BAND: |sigma_h| / scale <= 1e-10 for all 8 (domain, lane) pairs. `scale` is the natural stress unit of the kernel (`factor * c0`), so the band is dimensionless and independent of the material numbers.

Second assertion in the same case, free and worth having -- linearity, which the replay test cannot see: doubling every node concentration must double the reported maximum for a NON-uniform profile. Fill node j with c0*(1 + 0.1*j), record sigma_h, refill with 2x, and REQUIRE the ratio is 2.0 to within 1e-13 relative. That catches a sign or factor slip in `factor` (SpmStress.hpp:138-139) that a single-point replay can absorb.

Both are pure array fills plus one kernel call -- no simulation, so the gate stays short.

